      "mathematical_findings": [
        "Finite Fubini uses the actual inclusive prime-divisor carrier and the same physicalDivisorSum, including modulus one and zero receivers. The lower polynomial is at most its zero/one roughness indicator, hence at most one; no nonnegativity or absolute centre bound is inferred.",
        "Subtracting the signed centre mass is handled in the correct lower-bound direction. The result is pi(N)*density(rho)+totalPiError(rho)-chenPrimeDivisorCount(N,N) <= actual sifted count. The primitive generic premise is discharged by actualLowerSmallRoughRho_minorant and by the independently rounded compiler rho_minorant.",
        "CurrentChenMeanLedger supplies exact Upsilon1/Upsilon2 cardinalities at a=417/5000 and h=19/125. Their original 3+1 combination costs at most 4*omega(N) for positive N. The existing logarithmic prime-factor bound pays this uniformly in singularNormalization, with the threshold before both policies and all compiler data.",
        "For 0<epsilon<1/8, D=N^(249/448), w=D^(epsilon^2), L=D^epsilon and cap=ceil(N^h) satisfy all stated gates for both starts. The theorem makes no unsupported physical-support-level claim about arbitrary policies.",
        "rawMain is the independent full even-exit density minus actual Euler-weighted roundingLoss and actual absolute rounded beta loss. Its lower bound is multiplied only by the nonnegative actual total prime count. C,K and the common N threshold occur before both policies and tau; C,K are auxiliary beta constants, not the manuscript global K.",
        "plainPolicy is exactly the parity-safe ordinary root when passed to fixedEvenRoughCoefficient. The inherited same-weight two-sided Rosser-minus limit applies with s=beta/u>=2 and the derived covering cap, giving (2*exp(-gamma)/u)*suzukiContinuousLowerFactor(beta/u). The joint 3+1 limit and even-N threshold preserve the actual singularSeries normalization.",
        "At beta=nu the h ratio is in [2,4], yielding 4*log(nu/h-1)/nu after exact exponential cancellation. The a ratio exceeds 4 and correctly retains the full Suzuki factor. Fixed beta below nu is allowed only while beta>=2h; no distribution theorem at nu is claimed.",
        "The report and registry preserve the exact originalGroupedStarts owner formula and the distinction from ordinary BV-level initial means and enhanced H/h defects. No enhanced empty-prefix h bank or old H248 insertion is used in the new source."
      ],
      "quantifier_and_assumption_audit": [
        "No hstarts conclusion, final coefficient bound, density-limit premise, sharp error-smallness assumption or final count licence is assumed by the concrete exports.",
        "Generic pointwise lemmas explicitly expose their minorant premise, then concrete raw/rounded exports discharge it using existing proof bodies.",
        "The density and centre thresholds are uniform before the policy/mesh variables because the displayed losses and signed errors remain explicit; this does not provide uniform smallness for an N-varying policy.",
        "No new external theorem input or axiom is added. Existing analytic source dependencies retain their own verification status."
      ],
      "remaining_internal_obligations": [
